#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "the page where the form shortcode is published. The plugin creates it on activation, and this is where you point it somewhere else if you move it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "what the button says at the end of the form, the one that registers the declaration."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "which law is cited to the customer on the confirmation screen. Spain has not transposed Directive (EU) 2023/2673 yet, so both options apply the same requirements today; the Spanish one also cites the TRLGDCU."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "The deadline and the record"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "How long the customer has, and what is kept of each declaration. Fourteen days is the legal minimum in the European Union: you can give more, never less."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "after these days the order no longer shows the withdrawal button. The form still accepts a late request, with a warning, because deciding whether it is out of time is yours to do, not the form's."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "days on top of the window, for the time a delivery takes or simply to be generous with your customer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "the date the count starts from: the completed date, which is the closest thing to the delivery date, or the order date. With an order that is not completed yet, the plugin falls back on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "keeps the address the declaration was sent from, as evidence of who sent it and when."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "keeps the browser identifier, for the same reason. Both are personal data: keep them only if you are going to use them, and say so in your privacy policy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "unchecked, uninstalling the plugin leaves the requests and the settings in place. Checked, it takes everything with it, and there is no going back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "What happens the moment a declaration arrives."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "the plugin registers its own Withdrawal requested status, so those orders can be filtered, sorted and bulk-edited with the usual WooCommerce tools. Leave it as it comes and the order is not touched."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "asks the customer for an account when the money cannot go back the way it came. The number is checked with its international control digits, travels with the request as banking data, is included in the privacy exporter and is deleted by the eraser. Only ask for it if you really need it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "a visitor who is not logged in gets a single-use link at the address on the order, and the request only counts once that link is opened. It keeps the date and time of the original submission, so nobody loses days of their period."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "Automation and emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "A withdrawal has two lives in parallel: the request, with its own status, and the WooCommerce order. Here the two are tied together so you do not have to update both by hand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "Mark as ... when order becomes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "one line per request status. Choose which order status moves it, and the request follows the order on its own. A refunded order marking the request as completed is the usual one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "Email when changed to ..."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "which status changes write to the customer. The content of those emails is edited where all the WooCommerce ones are, in WooCommerce > Settings > Emails."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "What can be withdrawn"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "The law leaves some things out of the right of withdrawal: something made to measure, something unsealed, digital content already downloaded. Each product carries its own type in the Withdrawal tab of its data, and a category can set it for everything inside it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "Withdrawal allowed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "the usual one, and what a product inherits when neither it nor its categories say otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "there is no right of withdrawal for this product, and the customer is told so before buying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "the right is lost once the download starts, provided the customer accepted it beforehand. This is the type that triggers the waiver at checkout."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "made to the customer's measure, so it is excluded by law."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "neither yes nor no: the request comes in and you decide. For the cases the law leaves to the condition of the goods."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "what each type says to the customer, on the product page between the price and the Add to cart button, and again inside the form. Leave a field empty to keep the translated text that comes with the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "Downloadable content loses the right of withdrawal only if the customer accepted it before the download started, and the shop can prove it. This checkbox at checkout is that proof."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "never, only on the products classified as digital content, or on every order. The middle one is the usual choice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "comes filled in with the acknowledgement text. Edit it to say it your way, or empty the field to go back to the one that comes with the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "The requests"
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "Every declaration your customers send is kept here, with its order, its date, the products it covers and what the customer wrote. It is the log you can show if you are ever asked to prove how you handled a withdrawal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "it has arrived and nobody has looked at it yet. It is the status every request is born in."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "the withdrawal is valid. From here the refund follows, through WooCommerce."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "out of time, excluded product or whatever the reason. Write the reason down, because the customer can ask for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/clases/class-apg-withdrawal-help.php
msgid "everything is done, refund included. If you set up the automation, a refunded order leaves its request like this on its own."
msgstr ""
